`Object.freeze` of a `{ a: f64 }` is not supported yet
an `Object.freeze` result where a `{ a: f64 }` is expected is not supported yet: its fields could be written there
`Object.assign` cannot add `b` to a `{ a: f64 }`: adding a field its type doesn't declare is not supported yet
`Object.create` with a prototype other than `null` is not supported yet
`Object.create(null)` makes a `Record<string, V>`: it needs a variable or parameter of that type
`Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty` as a value is not supported yet
`Object.getPrototypeOf` of a `Date` is not supported yet
`Object.getPrototypeOf` of a `{ a: f64 } | null` is not supported yet
`Object.prototype.toString.call` of a `ObjectPrototype` is not supported yet
`Object.isFrozen` is not supported yet
`Object.seal` is not supported yet
`structuredClone` of a `Record<string, f64>`, which holds a record, is not supported yet in a program that calls `Object.create(null)`
`Date.prototype` is not supported yet
